      "body": "## Problem\n\n`vllm bench serve` collects speculative-decoding (and diffusion) stats by scraping `{base_url}/metrics` before and after the run (`fetch_spec_decode_metrics` / `fetch_diffusion_metrics`). When the benchmark targets a **PD-disaggregated deployment through `vllm-router`**:\n\n- `{router}/metrics` is not proxied to the backends (it answers `405 Method Not Allowed`),\n- the actual `vllm:spec_decode_*` counters live on the **decode instance**,\n\nso `fetch_spec_decode_metrics` returns `None` and every PD benchmark silently loses the acceptance section — no error, no hint.\n\n## Change\n\nAdd an optional `--metrics-url` that overrides where server metrics are scraped from (defaults to the request base URL = previous behavior). For PD, point it at the decode instance.\n\n## Verification (two-node DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash P/D, vllm-router front-end, DSpark speculative decoding in both pools)\n\nWithout the flag (status quo):\n\n```\nSuccessful requests: 4        # ... but no Acceptance section at all\n```\n\nWith `--metrics-url http://<decode-node>:8123`:\n\n```\nSuccessful requests:                     4\nAcceptance rate (%):                     28.62\nAcceptance length:                       2.43\n  Position 0:                            60.24\n  Position 1:                            35.86\n  Position 2:                            21.89\n  Position 3:                            14.67\n  Position 4:                            10.41\n```\n\nAlso confirmed directly: `curl {router}/metrics` → `405`; `curl {decode}/metrics` → 8 `vllm:spec_decode_*` series present.\n",
